From 11dd97e0655d703f7fbc8639f16a4c3c6f506dc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:47:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] organizations: serve a cached organization only to its
 own tenant

GetByID answered from the organization cache whenever the cached row's
business unit matched the request, before the row-level-security scoped
query ran. A request scoped to one organization that asked for another
organization of its business unit (or any request without a tenant scope)
was served the other organization from the cache, though the database
would have refused it. The cache is now used only when the request's
tenant scope is that organization; otherwise the read goes to the scoped
query.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L7Gd5v8t2y7WHswGwtgbrn
---
